# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via *.local) for local dev.
# For the deployed build, set these as GitHub Actions repo secrets instead
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions) — see .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Setup steps (Google Cloud Console — console.cloud.google.com):
# 1. Create a project (or reuse one).
# 2. APIs & Services > Enabled APIs > enable "Google Drive API".
# 3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen:
#    - User type: External.
#    - Publishing status: keep it in "Testing" (do NOT publish).
#    - Test users: add ONLY your own Google account email here.
#      This is what actually enforces "only me" — Google itself refuses
#      the consent screen for any other account while in Testing status.
# 4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID:
#    - Application type: Web application.
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://flameheater.github.io
#    - No redirect URI needed (this app uses the token/implicit flow, not
#      the redirect-based auth code flow).
# 5. Copy the generated Client ID into VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL=
